  "summary": "Chehalis and Napavine police chiefs say their Flock Safety ALPR systems remain effective under Washington's new SB 6002 regulations, with only minor adjustments such as relocating a camera near a church and shorter retention periods. Chehalis has paused its custom plate-watch-list function due to a new 24-hour review requirement it lacks staff to meet, while Napavine's chief is considering expanding from three cameras.",
